think Lap index: last recorded rota read was item 2 (follow-our-compass) on the math lap; this lap is item 3, foundations/20260811-211431_the-lindy-effect-and-the-long-return.md. Deep-read it: the plainest words are the longest-lived; a thing that does not perish lengthens its expected future the longer it lasts. Money is exactly such a readout -- a price reads true for centuries -- so a currency corpus is the Lindy-first crux, not a fashion corpus.
